# Score comparison notebook

This notebook is used to **compare and visualise evaluation scores** across the three modelling strategies
(per-species, mixed-species, and domain-adaptive).

## Purpose

- Compare model performance across pipelines using pre-computed evaluation results
- Generate figures and tables used in the manuscript

This notebook **does not implement any evaluation logic**.
All metrics are computed by scripts in `evaluation/`.

## Inputs

- Evaluation outputs stored under `runs/`
- CSV files generated by `evaluation/score_all.py` (e.g. `scores.csv`)

The notebook assumes the standard directory structure described in the repository README.

## Workflow

- Load evaluation CSV files
- Aggregate scores by pipeline and species
- Compute summary statistics
- Visualise results as figures and tables

## Outputs

- Comparative plots of model performance
- Tables summarising evaluation metrics

These outputs correspond to figures and tables in the manuscript ("@@@").

## Notes

- This notebook is intended for inspection and figure generation only.
- It is not required to reproduce the numerical results.
- Any changes to evaluation metrics should be made in `evaluation/`, not in this notebook.

